# Mutation-testing binary facade (Phase 9, R4-Q1).
#
# Builds the pinned go-mutesting v2.7.9 binary hermetically via rules_go.
# go_deps generates BUILD files for every module fetched from go.mod, so the
# upstream cmd/go-mutesting go_binary resolves at
# @com_github_jonbaldie_go_mutesting_v2//cmd/go-mutesting (public visibility);
# this alias gives callers a stable //tools/mutesting label.
#
# The binary must build with cgo disabled: it links github.com/zimmski/osutil,
# whose cgo-gated capture_linux.go uses syscall.Dup2 (removed in Go 1.26).
# The mutesting binary only needs osutil.CopyFile and only ever execs `go test`
# subprocesses, so a pure (cgo-free) build is safe and selects the
# capture_notlinux.go variant. Callers pass the pure flag on the command line
# (the Makefile facade and mutate.yml do this for every invocation):
#
#   bazel run --@io_bazel_rules_go//go/config:pure //tools/mutesting -- ...
alias(
    name = "mutesting",
    actual = "@com_github_jonbaldie_go_mutesting_v2//cmd/go-mutesting",
)
